    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No — don't stack NSAIDs. Ibuprofen and naproxen work the same way in your body, so mixing them doesn't add relief, it just multiplies the risks: stomach bleeding, kidney strain, and GI complications. It's not a \"higher level of relief,\" it's a higher level of danger.\n\nIf you need more relief than ibuprofen alone, the smarter combo is an NSAID plus acetaminophen (Tylenol) — they work through different mechanisms, so they're safe to take together at proper doses. So: 400mg ibuprofen every 6-8 hours with food, plus 500-650mg acetaminophen every 6 hours (staying under 3,000mg/day of Tylenol), and you've got a legitimate multi-mechanism approach that will likely outperform the mega-dose you were planning.",
